# disclosure.zd — components that render (spec §14D.1).
#
# `components.zd` states the whole design, including the placements that
# need the RPC client and the durable store neither of which exists yet
# (§16.5, M6), so it typechecks and refuses to build. This file is the
# same design with `client` state only, so it compiles all the way to a
# bundle and renders — which is what the parity test drives.
#
# Three things it exists to demonstrate:
#
#   1. A component is used exactly where a built-in element is. `Counter`
#      and `Column` are written the same way.
#   2. Component-local state is per *instance*. The two `Counter`s below
#      count independently, and nothing in the program says so — it falls
#      out of the state being declared inside the component.
#   3. `children` are the nodes nested at the call site, placed wherever
#      the component's body names them.
#
# `Panel` used to hold a `state open` and an `if`, which was disclosure
# hand-rolled out of a signal and a conditional region. It is `Details`
# now, and the whole of what that changed is what is missing: no signal,
# no conditional, no handler, and no line of this file saying how a
# disclosure behaves. The browser opens it, closes it on a keypress,
# announces it as expanded or collapsed, expands it when find-in-page
# lands inside, and prints it open. None of that was reachable before and
# none of it can be hand-rolled correctly.

component Counter with label
    state count is client Whole starting 0

    Column
        Text label
        Text count
        Button "more"
            on click
                add 1 to count

component Panel with title, children
    Details
        Summary title
        children

view
    Column
        Heading "Two counters"

        Counter "left"
        Counter "right"

        Panel "details"
            Row
                Text "inside the panel"
